<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="Claude" version="26.0.0">
  <diagram name="AI Gateway - Entra ID agent identity flow" id="aigw-entra-agent-flow">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1880" pageHeight="2180" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="title" value="Azure Entra ID to AI Gateway: the complete agent identity flow" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="18" width="1200" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Every element on the path a single agent call takes, from the directory that was synced last night to the provider the gateway finally reaches. Entra ID appears in three places and means something different in each." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="50" width="1700" height="22" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ================= BAND A : control plane ================= -->

        <mxCell id="bandAbg" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="90" width="1840" height="228" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bandAhdr" value="A &#8212; CONTROL PLANE. Runs on a sync schedule, never on the request path." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="96" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="A1" value="&lt;b&gt;1. Azure Entra ID tenant&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Users and security groups. The system of record for who exists and who belongs to what.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Entra&#39;s first job of three. Okta and on-premises AD slot in here instead, unchanged downstream.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="122" width="430" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="A2" value="&lt;b&gt;2. Cloud Identity Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In Strata Cloud Manager. A cloud directory of type Azure AD, authorised against the tenant.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;User Identity Attribute: UPN or Mail.&lt;/b&gt; Choose Mail when the UPN is &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;user@tenant.onmicrosoft.com&lt;/font&gt; and the real address differs." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="516" y="122" width="430" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="A3" value="&lt;b&gt;3. AI Gateway Directory Sync&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;An administrator maps each CIE group to exactly one AI Gateway workspace. One group, one workspace.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Background sync provisions new members and deprovisions departed ones." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="996" y="122" width="400" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="A4" value="&lt;b&gt;4. Workspace membership&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each synced user is a workspace member holding a workspace role, keyed by the email the directory supplied.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#006DCC&quot;&gt;This list is the only thing step 9 compares the token against.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1446" y="122" width="398" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="eA12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="A1" target="A2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eA23" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="A2" target="A3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eA34" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="A3" target="A4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <!-- ================= BAND B : one-off configuration ================= -->

        <mxCell id="bandBbg" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="334" width="1840" height="216" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="bandBhdr" value="B &#8212; ONE-OFF CONFIGURATION. Three places, three different Entra objects. None of them is the other." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="340" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="B1" value="&lt;b&gt;App registration in Entra, for the agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gives the agent something to authenticate as. Client credentials for an unattended agent, on-behalf-of when a signed-in person is behind the call.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Entra&#39;s second job of three: token issuer.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="366" width="590" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="B2" value="&lt;b&gt;Admin Settings &#8594; Organisation &#8594; Authentication&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Paste the JWKS URL, or the static JWKS JSON. A comma-separated list is accepted and the keys are merged.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;https://login.microsoftonline.com/&amp;lt;tenant&amp;gt;/discovery/v2.0/keys&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="656" y="366" width="590" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="B3" value="&lt;b&gt;Gateway environment, hybrid and air-gapped only&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_ENABLED=ON&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ORGANISATIONS_TO_SYNC=&amp;lt;org&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;PORTKEY_CLIENT_AUTH=&amp;lt;token&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_LOCAL_AUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES=&#8230;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Gateway 2.5.0 or higher. Backend v1.13.0 or higher for air-gapped." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1276" y="366" width="568" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ================= BAND C : per request ================= -->

        <mxCell id="bandChdr" value="C &#8212; PER REQUEST. One agent call, start to finish." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="566" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S1" value="&lt;b&gt;1 &#183; The agent asks Entra for a token&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Client credentials for an unattended agent, or on-behalf-of to carry a signed-in person. Nothing about the gateway is involved yet." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="594" width="820" height="78" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S2" value="&lt;b&gt;2 &#183; Entra returns a signed JWT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Header carries &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;alg: RS256&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;typ: JWT&lt;/font&gt; and a &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;kid&lt;/font&gt;. Payload carries at minimum &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;iss&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;aud&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;sub&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;exp&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;You cannot add gateway-specific claims to a stock Entra token. That is what makes this a Mode B integration.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="696" width="820" height="100" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S3" value="&lt;b&gt;3 &#183; The agent sends the inference call&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;x-portkey-api-key: &amp;lt;raw JWT&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;JWT&amp;gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;Do not write the word Bearer inside &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot; color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;x-portkey-api-key&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;. That is the single most common setup failure.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="820" width="820" height="100" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S4" value="&lt;b&gt;4 &#183; The gateway decides where to validate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A JWT-shaped token on Cloud goes to the management plane. On hybrid or air-gapped with &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_ENABLED=ON&lt;/font&gt; the data plane verifies it itself and keeps working while the management plane is unreachable." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="944" width="820" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S5" value="&lt;b&gt;5 &#183; Signature and header checks against the JWKS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;kid&lt;/font&gt; must resolve to a key in the JWKS. &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;alg&lt;/font&gt; must be &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;RS256&lt;/font&gt;, the RSA key must be 2048-bit or larger, and &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;exp&lt;/font&gt; must be in the future. Small clock skew is tolerated.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;Every failure here is written to the audit log and returned to the caller as an invalid-key error.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1058" width="820" height="106" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S6" value="&lt;b&gt;6 &#183; Resolve the organisation and the workspace&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organisation: &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey_oid&lt;/font&gt; or &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;organisation_id&lt;/font&gt; from the token, otherwise &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ORGANISATIONS_TO_SYNC&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;Workspace: &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey_workspace&lt;/font&gt; or &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;workspace_slug&lt;/font&gt; from the token, otherwise the first entry in the workspace allowlist, otherwise the organisation default workspace." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1188" width="820" height="106" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S7" value="&lt;b&gt;7 &#183; Resolve the scopes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;From the token&#39;s &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;scope&lt;/font&gt; string or &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;scopes&lt;/font&gt; array, otherwise from &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_LOCAL_AUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES&lt;/font&gt;. A chat completion needs &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;completions.write&lt;/font&gt;. The &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey.&lt;/font&gt; prefix is optional." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1318" width="820" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S8" value="&lt;b&gt;8 &#183; Read the identity out of the claims&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The gateway takes the first claim present, in this order:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;email_id&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;sub&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;uid&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;That value is what per-user logging and per-user metrics are keyed on." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1432" width="820" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S9" value="&lt;b&gt;9 &#183; One string comparison&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Does that email match a workspace member from band A, step 4?" style="rhombus;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1546" width="820" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S9yes" value="&lt;b&gt;Match&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The call is attributed to that person and inherits their workspace role. Logs, metrics and per-user budgets all resolve to a human being." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1700" width="396" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S9no" value="&lt;b&gt;No match&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The call falls back to a generic workspace service key. &lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;It still succeeds. No error is returned, and the only symptom is attribution that quietly stops naming anyone.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#ef4444;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="460" y="1700" width="396" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S10" value="&lt;b&gt;10 &#183; Policy, limits and the log record&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Workspace usage limits, rate limits, budget policies and guardrails run against whatever identity step 9 settled on. The log entry is written with the same value." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#006DCC;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1884" width="820" height="86" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="S11" value="&lt;b&gt;11 &#183; Egress, on a completely different credential&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The gateway calls Azure AI Foundry with the credential held in its own provider configuration: an API key, or an Entra service principal or managed identity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;The agent&#39;s token never leaves the gateway. Foundry sees the gateway, not the agent, and not the person.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Entra&#39;s third job of three.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1998" width="820" height="112" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="e12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S1" target="S2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e23" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S2" target="S3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e34" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S3" target="S4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e45" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S4" target="S5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e56" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S5" target="S6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e67" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S6" target="S7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e78" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S7" target="S8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e89" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S8" target="S9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e9yes" value="yes" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;fontSize=10;fontColor=#333333;fontFamily=Helvetica;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S9" target="S9yes"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e9no" value="no" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#ef4444;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;fontSize=10;fontColor=#333333;fontFamily=Helvetica;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S9" target="S9no"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eY10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.25;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S9yes" target="S10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eN10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.75;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S9no" target="S10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e1011" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S10" target="S11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="eA4S9" value="compared against" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;endArrow=blockThin;endFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;fontSize=10;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;verticalAlign=bottom;" edge="1" parent="1" source="A4" target="S9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1645" y="558"/><mxPoint x="876" y="558"/><mxPoint x="876" y="1601"/></Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ================= RIGHT COLUMN : reference panels ================= -->

        <mxCell id="P1" value="&lt;b&gt;The three Entra objects, side by side&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Source directory&lt;/b&gt; (band A). Configured in Strata Cloud Manager, under Cloud Identity Engine. Decides who is a workspace member. Never consulted during a request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Token issuer&lt;/b&gt; (band B, step 1). Configured as an app registration in Entra plus a JWKS URL in the gateway. Consulted on every request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Egress credential&lt;/b&gt; (step 11). Configured on the gateway&#39;s Azure provider. The caller never sees it and cannot influence it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#006DCC&quot;&gt;All three can point at the same Entra tenant. They are still three separate configurations, and breaking one does not break the others.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="594" width="948" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P2hdr" value="What the token can and cannot carry" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="812" width="948" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P2a" value="&lt;b&gt;Mode A &#8212; you control the issuer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;{&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;sub&quot;: &quot;agent-7&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;email_id&quot;: &quot;ana@corp.com&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;portkey_oid&quot;: &quot;org_abc&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;portkey_workspace&quot;: &quot;ws_ai&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;scope&quot;: &quot;completions.write&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;usage_limits&quot;: { &#8230; },&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;rate_limits&quot;: { &#8230; },&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;exp&quot;: 1767225600&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Org, workspace, scopes and limits all travel in the token. Nothing has to be configured on the gateway side." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="836" width="462" height="340" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P2b" value="&lt;b&gt;Mode B &#8212; a stock Entra token&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;{&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;iss&quot;: &quot;https://login.micro&#8230;&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;aud&quot;: &quot;api://ai-gateway&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;sub&quot;: &quot;a1b2c3d4&#8230;&quot;,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&quot;exp&quot;: 1767225600&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;Entra is named in the product documentation as a Mode B case, alongside Okta, Auth0 and Cognito.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Organisation comes from &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ORGANISATIONS_TO_SYNC&lt;/font&gt;, workspace from deployment settings, scopes from the IdP registration or &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_LOCAL_AUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES&lt;/font&gt;, limits from the workspace." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1382" y="836" width="462" height="340" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P3" value="&lt;b&gt;Where step 5 actually runs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI Gateway Cloud.&lt;/b&gt; The management plane validates every token. Nothing to configure beyond the JWKS URL.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Hybrid and air-gapped.&lt;/b&gt; Set &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_ENABLED=ON&lt;/font&gt; and the data plane verifies locally, which removes a management-plane round trip from every call and keeps authentication working through a control-plane outage. Leave it off and JWT-shaped tokens go to the management plane as before.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;JWKS fetches honour &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;HTTPS_PROXY&lt;/font&gt; and &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;TLS_CA&lt;/font&gt;, so an egress-restricted gateway can still reach Entra." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="1208" width="948" height="176" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P4" value="&lt;b&gt;Failure modes worth knowing before you debug one&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;HS256 instead of RS256&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; rejected, and the error reads like a bad API key rather than a bad algorithm.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Missing or unresolvable &lt;/b&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;kid&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; &#8212; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;Error Verifying JWT token: Signing Key Not Found&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bearer written inside &lt;/b&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;x-portkey-api-key&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; &#8212; send the raw token there, or use the &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;Authorization&lt;/font&gt; header instead.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Private key pasted into the JWKS&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; the JWKS holds public key parameters only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;JWKS URL unreachable&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; the gateway has to be able to fetch it, which an egress policy can quietly prevent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Entra omits &lt;/b&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;alg&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;b&gt; on its JWKS keys&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; fixed in v2.1.0, which falls back to RS256. Older builds fail here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scope missing&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a perfectly valid token still gets refused. Entra generally cannot issue &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;completions.write&lt;/font&gt;, so &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_LOCAL_AUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES&lt;/font&gt; is usually required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Empty identity attribute&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a user whose chosen UPN or Mail attribute is blank is skipped during CIE sync, silently, and then never matches at step 9.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;All invalid-JWT errors land in the audit log, with the token redacted to its first and last few characters.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#ef4444;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="1416" width="948" height="256" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P5" value="&lt;b&gt;If none of this is what you wanted&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;An unattended agent with no person behind it has no email to match, so step 9 will always fall through. Give that agent its own workspace service key and name it in &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;x-portkey-metadata&lt;/font&gt;, rather than building a token flow that attributes every call to the same generic key." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="1704" width="948" height="116" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="P6" value="&lt;b&gt;Where identity forwarding stops&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everything above decides what the &lt;i&gt;gateway&lt;/i&gt; knows about the caller. None of it reaches the model provider, and only some of it reaches a downstream tool.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;MCP Gateway&lt;/b&gt; can forward caller identity to an MCP server three ways: a claims header, passing the original bearer token through, or a gateway-signed JWT in a header you name.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Agent Gateway (A2A)&lt;/b&gt; has no equivalent. A client authenticates with a gateway API key carrying the &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;agents.invoke&lt;/font&gt; scope, and access control is per agent and per skill. Per-user access control for agents is listed as coming soon.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;So an A2A call can be attributed, but it cannot carry the caller&#39;s identity onward to the agent it invokes.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="1852" width="948" height="258" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
